{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345182",
      "title": "Arrow Functions",
      "sourceHash": "0570ffedb4bdc2ec66b249de845791aaf61aa7b505552703e228e722d9db59ba",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.01,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "Now what you see here is one way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 5.94,
          "en": "of defining a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 8.73,
          "en": "but I'm going to comment out this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.73,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "for the moment because there also is an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "In JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "you can also create so-called arrow functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "a syntax that's especially popular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 20.91,
          "en": "if you're dealing with anonymous functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 23.07,
          "en": "a function that don't need a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.07,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "For example, here in this React app I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "in the first course section, you might remember",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "that on the buttons we had this on click attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 36.81,
          "en": "and we used some React syntax to point at a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.81,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "that should be executed when the button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "And for that here I used this arrow function syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "to define a function in the place where it's needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 50.01,
          "en": "as a value for this click listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.01,
          "end": 52.38,
          "en": "And this is a so-called anonymous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.38,
          "end": 54.45,
          "en": "because it doesn't carry any name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.45,
          "end": 56.463,
          "en": "It's just the function code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "Now, anonymous functions can also be defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.33,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "with the function keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 64.57,
          "en": "You can define functions like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 68.553,
          "en": "and for example, console log Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.45,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "And we could then, for example, export this as a default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 75.06,
          "en": "if we wanted to, and we would now be exporting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 79.023,
          "en": "a so-called anonymous function which doesn't carry any name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.34,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "But if you are dealing with such anonymous functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 86.07,
          "en": "you can use the arrow function syntax as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "since this is a bit shorter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 89.67,
          "en": "When using arrow functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "you omit the function keyword, you must not use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "and you instead just have your parameter list here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 99.45,
          "en": "like for example, username and message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "This doesn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "Then you have this arrow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "and then you have the curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 106.32300000000001,
          "en": "which contain the function body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "You can also still use the return keyword here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 114.21000000000001,
          "en": "if you want to, and that's how you would define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.21000000000001,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "using this arrow function syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "In this course, you'll see both kinds of functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "using the function keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "and using this arrow function notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 127.62,
          "en": "Ultimately, it is up to you which approach you prefer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.62,
          "end": 129.363,
          "en": "but you should know about both.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}